   151	- **The shelf** is the second camp past the Line and the first fire (#46). **The Velmere letter** stays sealed on Brom's table at Halcenvane; it is not carried. **Seln's case** came east in his own satchel and rides under the canvas from the shelf.
   152	- **Shadow's first Book 7 use** is restaged so Oryn cannot see or attribute it (audit B2). **#23** (sell the cart and gelding in Lowmarch's first week; the money is a sealed reserve) is treated as binding.
   153	
   154	## 49. Book 7 — protected Quiet-line / Kindling wording (OWNER ITEM; needed before Book 7 Movement 4)
   155	Seven protected lines say variants of "mine didn't", "my Path", "mine has been asleep since I was fourteen", "dark since fourteen", "every Path … his had not". Edition canon (Book 6): Cael's own Arbiter woke at Kindling, the plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and the Arbiter went dark; he has no Path. At a Quiet line the others' live Arbiters stop, his is dark before and after, and his fragments still answer. **Default until ruled: the protected lines stay verbatim**, the surrounding plan and prose state the canon, and the lines read as Cael's own shorthand. Options: (1) release only the conflicting clauses for a minimal canon repair; (2) release the affected log entries for clean re-composition; (3) keep as is (the default).
   156	
   157	## 50. Book 7 — "Six years I've wanted a face" (OWNER ITEM; needed before Book 7 Movement 7)
   158	The protected line gives Seln six years; edition Book 6 has him carry the case twelve years (fifteen in service). **Default until ruled: the line stays verbatim** and the plan stops calling the case a six-year matter. Options: (1) "Twelve years I've wanted a face."; (2) "All these years I've wanted a face."; (3) keep six and name a separate event six years back that began the wish.

