    92	## After
    93	
    94	- **The bowman** comes down to the water when it is over, counts five, and says "none of you shouted"; he says it again in the barn.
    95	- **The steading's woman** binds four of five and says the protected "Four," … "Out of five. Two men went down to that ford this month and one came up." She marks the slip on the bowman's word.
    96	- **The finding** is dictated by Karis and written by Cael in Hesk's book, the night of the 53rd, because it will not keep and she cannot hold a pencil: discharge; hearing and sight used only to keep station and to try a quiet body; water masks it (a wading hound goes to where the declaration was; a Path under water an hour and a quarter drew nothing at eleven feet); no leader, only a first mover; they learn. Not accounted for: 110 yards; dusk. She does not look at the book; he reads it back.
    97	- **The seal entry** (protected) closes the day-53 log, then *Deployment since the Line: one.*
    98	- **Pike's ford line** (protected) comes up by carter on the 57th and is printed once, there. Under it the protected *First honest number…* entry. Its saying at the book on the 60th is narration.
