   128	## State at movement end (for the ledger)
   129	
   130	**Calendar.** The evening of the **sixty-ninth day past the Line**, under the lower inn's eave at Lowmarch. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("the thaw" in three places; "frost" once). Days on the page: 51, 52, 53, 54, 55–57 (the stick on the 56th; the carter back on the 57th), 58, 59, 60, 61, 62, 63, 64, 65, 66, 68, 69. Told, not shown: the dusk of the 49th at the ford; the 50th. Weather: dry roads; mist on the river at first light; cold coming up out of the wash after dark. The next movement opens on the morning of day 70.
   131	
   132	**Where everyone is.** All five at Lowmarch, sleeping in the meadow, with the three boxes in the loft over the ferryman's drum. Teague and his three are out on two holds' slips up the north water.
   133	
   134	**Cael.** Eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments and the uncounted anomaly.** **Deployment since the Line: one** (a single Wind burst at the ford on day 53, in front of the hold's bowman). Shadow unused; it lifted at dusk through the wait at the ford and again on the walk down the bar and was refused. Ember offered a point in the hound's mouth over Karis and was refused. The Iron read stays shut. Left calf bitten through on day 53: a leg on level ground, nine strides uphill. He has not asked Seln for his report, has not answered Lira's question, has not answered Hesk's letter, and has stopped counting Lira's runs. He knows that he had a grandmother who crossed the Line once on a trade run; no name, no line of descent.
   135	
   136	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. Right ankle: ligaments, never seen by a healer, bound eleven days; no stick since day 64; runs on the gravel bar from day 65; "it bends less, and later". No burst at the ford or since. She killed one hound with the long knife. Her question stands unanswered in Cael's log.
   137	
   138	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. He declared once at the ford, on purpose, for about three breaths, and dropped it with the hound's teeth shut on his arm; he drowned that hound with his shoulder and the current. Left forearm: closed clean on day 66, re-wrapped by his own choice, "shut, not sound". He has carried nothing since day 53. He keeps Pike's six words ("Same as anyone. What'd he do?") on a dead slip inside his shirt.
   139	
   140	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. One point lit and put out at the ford; none since. Two pink lines across each palm; a pencil again on day 68. Holds: the hypothesis leaf; the finding (in Cael's log, by her dictation, and in the field archive in Lira's hand); a leaf headed *This side.*; the carter's map; and, in the middle box, the carter's wife's three sentences with *everybody knows* underlined twice. She has asked nobody what quiet ground is, Seln included.
   141	
   142	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze (not said in public). Lifted his Path once, under water, on day 53; killed the seventh hound. Unmarked. Walked the south road to the well first, alone, and said nothing. Has said aloud that he keeps waiting to be asked for his report. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut**; it spent the evening of day 53 in Thornwater's loft.
   143	
   144	**Objects and money.** Three boxes over the ferry drum. The reserve unopened. Board purse: **sixty-two marks earned** (18 + ford 40 + well 4); **fifty-two in hand** (one mark on flour and bacon on day 51; one to the hold for linen and thread; coppers unitemised). Hesk's satchel holds the log (with the finding and the seal entry), the old volume, the observation notebook, Pike's two lines on bark, and Hesk's letter. Cael's coat has lost its left sleeve. The ash stick is propping an old carter's shaft under the ash.
   145	
   146	**Pike's book and the wall.** **Six lines** under the five names: the protected ford line (said on day 60) and *The well at the south fork. Air cleared, shaft drawn, six stones set. Four marks.* (day 64). **Twelfth of thirteen; Teague eleven up.** The ford slip is with the finished slips, struck with one line through Teague's name and five strokes beneath, and Thornwater's mark at the foot. Fourteen slips on the plank on day 60; a bare tack set by the left-hand post on the evening of day 69 for a hold's slip expected from the north-west.
   147	
   148	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five, and nobody else. The hold's bowman saw one Wind burst and took it for a Path. The party now holds the stillhound finding in five sentences. **Quiet ground is three sentences from a carter's wife**; nobody has asked Pike or anyone. Thornwater knows the five as the crew that came up from its ford. Teague has read the struck slip and the line and said nothing; no meeting.
   149	
   150	**Open threads.** Two hounds gone down the river, logged as open. Why a hundred and ten yards; why dusk. What quiet ground is, and what a road bends round two days east of Thornwater. Lira's question. Hesk's letter and the roof. What Teague will say when they have cost him something. A hold's slip, with a ford in it, due on the oak in the morning.
