    88	
    89	- **Where Thornwater's ford lies (flag):** the upper of the two shallow crossings of the valley's water that the party made on day 43; below the mouth of the stretch; between two and three hours' walk below the gate. The pack that paced the cart on the stretch is the ford's pack.
    90	- **The ford's ground (flag):** a river some fifty yards wide over a single ledge of grey rock, **the sill**, ten feet broad, with two wheel-grooves and green slime; shin-deep fast water over it; a slow glide above; below, a **lip**, and pools that fall away over a man's head. A gravel **bar** in mid-river, thirty yards by eight, lying with the stream, its blunt head at the sill and its tail running down between the two pools to a point. A near (Thornwater-side) and a far channel, twenty yards each; a near and a far beach; a cut bank a man's height above the near beach.
    91	- **The lip stones (flag):** a row of white stones, a yard apart, which the hold sets along the sill's downstream lip each year "when the water drops", so that a wheel can see where the rock stops. Five yards of the row were unset on day 52; the row is whole by day 58.
    92	- **The third (flag):** two men of the hold went down at noon on the 49th to set the last stones. One, a Force, lifted with his Path under water to free the other's leg and was let alone; he stood up on the dry bar at dusk and was taken. The other got his hand between a hound's jaws and his own throat, was left when the Force shouted, and walked home in the dark. Neither is named.
    93	- **What the hold knows:** "Dusk. Never noon."; the bowman has had the gate-walk thirty years, has seen one come up the grass four evenings in five, and **set the white stone himself in his first year, where they stop**. He cannot say why there. The 110 yards stay unaccounted for.
    94	- **The finding (flag), as dictated by Karis and written in Cael's log:** the stillhound hunts Path discharge; it hears and sees a little, and uses both only to keep its place and to try a quiet body with its teeth; water masks it at both ends (a wading hound goes to where the declaration was when it left dry ground; a Path held under water for an hour and a quarter drew nothing at eleven feet); there is no leader, only whichever moves first; they learn. Not accounted for: 110 yards; dusk.
    95	- **"Discharge"** is Karis's lecturer's word for what leaves a person when a Path is used; assessors call it presence and mark it; a station reads it off a plate.
    96	- **A fragment answering is felt by Cael as something going out**, like the others' discharge. Whether a hound can tell it from a Path is untested; he holds on the supposition that it cannot. The one burst drew three.
    97	- **Seven hounds at the ford:** six that lie up in the far bank's grass and come down by three paths; a seventh, older, white-muzzled, with a torn left ear, that lies on the bar's tail. They drink one at a time and will not wet a foot.
    98	- **Seln's Path under water (flag):** on day 53 he lifts his own Shadow for the first time since the crossroads fire, to the chin in the near pool, and lets it go before he rises. His knife: narrow, dull, a hand long. "The cut" is his trade's word for the man placed where the subject will run.
    99	- **The hold's arrangements:** the bowman goes down as the hirer's witness and stands on the cut bank; the carter waits with the cart at the last bend; Seln's case stays in the loft between the second box and the third for that one evening.
