   213	"Then it's a complaint. Against himself."
   214	
   215	"It may be. I'll take it, though." Brom walked a little way. "I've been told what I was worth by a district panel and a provincial counter and a letter with a red seal on it. That's the first time anybody ever said it and thought he'd had the better of the bargain."
   216	
   217	They had started late, and dusk caught them four miles short of the meadow.
