    10	
    11	They passed the split shaft, pointing at the sky, and the stony swell, and came to the gully's fan, where the pale stones lay across the valley under a skin of water. Karis stopped there. She stood in the middle of the wet with her boots in it and looked down, and then to the right, at the slope that a grey thing had climbed sooner than set one foot where she was standing; and she wrote a single word, walking, and shut the book.
    12	
    13	There was nothing beside the white stone, and the gate was open before they reached it.
    14	
