    52	
    53	"You'll ask me what you want to know," she said. "I've hired you, and a hired crew's got a right. I'd tell a fencer where the ground was soft."
    54	
    55	Karis had drawn her notebook out; she looked round at fourteen faces, and laid it on her knee, shut, with one finger in it.
    56	
    57	"Tell us what you'd tell anyone you'd sent down there," said Cael.
