editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:108:7. **Seam repairs staged as scenes (+5,000).** The horse, cart and purse (C1). Oryn leaving her mule with the crew at Thornwater (C2). Karis pacing the Stair's perimeter on the morning of the 115th and laying the cord at the Hall on the 120th, so that Ch23's "paced two and cord-measured the third" is true on the page (C3).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:137:Close third, **Cael ≈259,700 words (≈86.6%)**. Five named cutaway characters at ≈40,000 total, plus Vastin's canonical three sentences (≈300). Total secondary ≈40,300 (≈13.4%). Every window is brief, purposeful, set inside a Cael-dominant chapter, and never an alternating chapter.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:156:Formula §5: the protagonist gets **≈135 growth beats** (4.5 per 10k; one about every 2,200 words), spread evenly with a slight middle bump. By movement: M1 14 · M2 15 · M3 17 · M4 18 · M5 19 · M6 18 · M7 17 · M8 17. By thirds that is ≈42 / 48 / 45. Supporting characters get many small beats each (0.1–0.7 per 10k = 3–21 over the book). No deuteragonist.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:178:**Density targets** (≈58 per 10k overall, front-loaded about 1.7x): **first third ≈81 per 10k** (M1 ≈82, M2 ≈82, M3 ≈78); **middle third ≈48** (M4 ≈50, with the line's mechanics taught as trials; M5 ≈42, with the acquisition spike; M6 ≈40); **final third ≈46** (M7 ≈40, M8 ≈55 with the inventory and the map). After M4 the system surfaces only at genuine turns: the notice, the self-readings, the rim, the fixed point, the inventory.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:180:**How the first third teaches hard without spending anything:** the log's inventory of nine, with each fragment's idle rent named (Shadow at dusk, Anchor wanting doorways, Storm heavy); the discipline of holding as a skill with failure modes; the board's arithmetic (outcome, not tier); the carters' "don't declare"; the ford's discharge finding; the shale-backs' flight; Oryn's Tide taught in full (contact only, the reserve, three mendings a day, cannot heal herself, "cannot mend what I can't read," two readings); tier talk at the plank (Pike's Copper Force, Teague's unreported Bronze, Lira's Iron R1, Brom's Copper forever). **Cael deploys nothing in M1–M3 except the single ford burst.** The log reads "Deployment since the Line: one" from day 53 to day 90, and the edition keeps that count.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:192:| **Tide-adjacent (NEW, the tenth)** | M5 day 100 the deep reading; **the notice** (verbatim, §10); M6 cost: three days of *listening*, not pulling (his own current at the edge of thought; the nine audible as flows); the idle state learned by the third night; **the first self-reading** (a place near the middle that does not flow; location only; not named); M7 ask refused at the lean-to, granted on the road; the first reading of another person (Oryn: banks, one channel, a current that runs *to* things); M8 the second and third self-readings; **"the still place"** (the phrase appears first here); told to Oryn with his hand on her wrist; **Teague not read** | Contact only; surface at a count of ten, deep only with the subject still, whole and willing; does nothing in a fight; *ask first, every time*; "Things you keep touching don't heal" |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:196:**Others' progression:** Lira learns to be fast with nothing at the end (M2), and learns to shoot braced one-armed (M6 → M8). Brom learns Iron Skin is a shout out here, and what he is without it ("a big man with good footwork and a lip of fused stone"). Karis learns to keep one point; the lattice line across a mountain; the wall along a line from her knees. Seln learns that his Path "was never most of what I do." Oryn: what her hands can and cannot do at a line, tested eight times alone. Teague: a column he does not have.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:258:- The kit's last line (Ch20): *third site confirmed on bearing* —
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:264:- Ephram (Ch9), whole letter: *Cael — / Weather first, because you'll want it in order, and I've watched you want things in order. / The Crown yard has a new cohort captain. The intake came up the bluff a fortnight ago, forty-one of them, and they've put a third-year over them who was a second-year when you left and whose name you would not know, so I'll not spend the ink. He is fair. He counts slower than you did. They stand where he puts them. / Withrow's tenure holds. That is the whole of the sentence. I asked whether there was a longer one and was told there was not, in a way that meant there had been, for a week. / A query came down to the registry from somewhere above it. Bracken would not say where and I did not ask twice. It wanted former enrollees' last known direction of travel. Bracken answered it. He gave them a map reference to the Line and nothing past it — which is true, and which Bracken enjoyed being true. He told me so at the plaque wall with his hands behind his back, and then told me he had not told me. / I still lose to you every time I run it. I have stopped running it in the yard. / Rooke says the yard's quieter. He didn't say it was worse. He also didn't say it wasn't. / — E.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:274:- Ch3, the seal: *Seln did the shadow work tonight. I didn't. Out here there's a ledger and a ferry west once a month, and a defector's tradecraft in my hands would tell anyone who reads carefully where I learned it. The seal holds. Different country, same arithmetic.* — and *First honest number anyone's written about us in a year. It says four of five got hurt. It's right.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:301:- Ch4: the carter's wife: "You mean the quiet ground? Everybody knows the quiet ground. Nobody goes in." — Lira: "So what am I becoming, exactly, if nobody's measuring?" — Seln: "I keep waiting for someone to ask for my report." — Brom: "What does the board pay a man with no Path at all." / Pike: "Same as anyone," … "What'd he do?" — Pike: "Teague's still eleven up. He'll speak to you when you've cost him something. That's not rudeness. That's the ledger."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:310:- Ch13: Oryn: "You don't get a yes. You get told." — Karis: "Ephram fought you in earnest and the notice said non-hostile. This is earnest and it isn't a fight at all." … "The model doesn't say the engagement has to be a fight. It says it has to be real." — Seln: "That's not consent. It's the nearest thing to it the log's ever had, and it's still not it. I'd enter both." — Lira: "She asked to read you," … "She didn't ask for the rest. Those aren't the same sentence." — Oryn's twenty-minute report: "I can feel that there's movement. More than one. I can't count them — I can't find where one stops. There's no channel. Everyone has a channel; I feel the banks and I know the Path. I can't find the banks in you. I've looked for twenty minutes. It isn't that you're broken. It's that I can't find anything shaped like the thing I read." — "Eleven years. I've never had my hands in something and not known what it was." — "Something just changed," she said. "In you. While I was in there." / "Yes." / "Did I do that?" / "No. I did." … "I need to tell you what I am." / "Then lie still while you do it. You've been still for twenty minutes. I want to see if you can manage twenty-one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:312:- Ch15: *the Quieting* — "A personal spiritual entity should not fail the way five looms fail when somebody shuts the sluice on the wheel that drives them." — *identically* — Seln: "Six sigils on the road that day," … "Five went out." … "I'm not filing that either. I'm counting it." — Karis's struck six: *one dark since fourteen; no change either side of the line; stated by him, not tested by me* — **The stratum limit, the book's only [UNBOUND]:** "It's older, I'll say once and not again, than [UNBOUND] — older than the word they retired, and I can't say by how much. Entered as a limit, not a finding. We explained the middle of the story in Ostrand. This is before the beginning, and I don't have a ruler for it." — Brom: "Say it with less." / Karis: "Everything I can date, I've dated. The floor's under all of it. I don't know how far." — "I have a hypothesis and I'm not entering it, because entering it would make it a finding, and it isn't one. It's a fear." … Lira: "Does it help? Not writing it." / "No," Karis said. "It's just correct." — "The circle's perfect," … "Perfect isn't natural. Somebody made a floor that turns Paths off. It's older than anything I can date. And it doesn't turn you off. Three facts. I'm not putting a verb between them." … "I'm not," Karis said. "I'm saying it to you. That's different." [OWNER-pending #49]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:313:- Ch16: Lira: "You told me when you knew. You don't know. So you told me *that*. Keep doing it." … "It scares you." / "Out there I was the thing the system couldn't hold." … "In there I was the only thing that *worked*. I don't know which one's worse." / "The second one. You're allowed to say so." — Seln: "They know something turns Paths off. They *don't* know something doesn't turn off. Yet." — Oryn: "My hands stop at that line. Yours don't. I had my hands in you for twenty minutes and I can tell you what I didn't find, which is a Path. That's all I've got." … "I'm not going to guess past it." — Karis: "We find the others. All of them. And we find out whether they're the same." … "That's how you find a handful. One at a time, for money." — Oryn: "Don't go in without me. Not because I'm any use inside. Because somebody should be outside the line who can put an arm back on." — Brom: "That's not comfort," … "I don't do that. It's a count. You like counts." — Oryn: "Once is a morning." … "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:318:- Ch21: Oryn: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole." — Seln: "It's blind. It reads weight on the floor. It strikes where the weight is. And it strikes what *stays*." — Karis: "It reads that as the heaviest thing on the floor," / Cael: "It reads that as the thing that *stays*," — Lira: "We're going in without Paths to look at walls with a thing under the floor." / "Yes," Karis said. / "Just checking that's the plan." — Seln: "It's blind. It reads the floor. Get *off* the floor." — "You're copying," / "I'm not getting another chance," / "No, I can see that you're not," — *A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest.* — "Brom," Cael said. "Wall. Your weight. Now." — Oryn: "Twice. It'll hold twice. It will not hold three times this season, so don't ask it to" — "You went in the water." / "You went in for Brom." / "Brom's on my route." … "So are you." … "Lie still. I want to read you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:352:- **C3 · Karis's measurements.** Ch23: "I've paced two and cord-measured the third." The Stair's perimeter was never paced on the page (Ch18: "I'll pace it in the morning", and the morning was the trap). At the Hall she stood "with the cord in her hand and not laid" (Ch21). **Recommend:** stage the Stair pacing on the morning of day 115 under Teague's rim watch, and the Hall's cord laid during the two marsh days (119–120). Ch23's sentence and the bible's "same radius at the Long Stair and the Drowned Hall" then become true on the page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:20:> - **Asset state after #23:** no cart or horse; the reserve is sealed under masonry chips in the third box and opens only by all five; the boxes lodge over the ferry drum when the crew is near Lowmarch; Seln's closed case is back on its strap (`manuscript/chapter-03.md:107,123-185`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:277`; `manuscript/chapter-05.md:55-65`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:39:- **"Ford's had a third."** Pike draws **one** line through Teague's name and writes five underneath: "That's arithmetic I can't do yet." Cael notices that a man never once made wrong by a crew has just written the line that might.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:41:- **The loft:** Seln's seven, and the cut dog that is never the one you're looking at. **Karis's hypothesis** (discharge; water masks it; "Evidence against: none, which I don't trust."). The plan: **bait with one declaration and kill with everything that isn't one.** "Never two at once, never the same person twice."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:46:- **Lowmarch, day 60:** fourteen slips. Seln reads the board and takes the well: "I keep waiting for someone to ask for my report." **Brom at the plank's end:** "What does the board pay a man with no Path at all." / "Same as anyone… What'd he do?" He writes it on an old slip and keeps it against his skin, the second time in his life (Rooke was the first). Pike: "Held a dog with a shoulder and a river, that one." **The mail** sorted aloud. Hesk's letter (protected), and the grandmother he did not know about. The log. **The saying** at the book, the sheet rewritten by hand: twelfth. "Teague's still eleven up. He'll speak to you when you've cost him something."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:47:- **New on the page, days 61–69, the well on the south road.** Seln walks it first and says nothing. A small physical job with a real, mundane hazard (your choice: bad air, a stuck windlass, a fouled shaft; no monster). Four marks. Lira leans the stick against the inn wall on day 64 and walks off. Her first runs on an ankle that bends "less, and later"; fast still, with no one counting. Brom's wrist closes clean on day 66; he looks at it with the lock face and wraps it again. The money is honest (48 → 52 by the movement's end).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:26:- **The telling on the table** is explicitly a retelling to Oryn of what Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln already established in edition B6: his own Arbiter woke at Kindling; the station plate lit eleven seconds late; the failed-safe word replaced the old name; the Arbiter then went dark. Sources are named by Path, not by person, except the three Oryn has touched. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B4, B7] The notice said aloud. The page fetched from the loft and read twice in its counted places. **Her answer** (protected): "So I couldn't read you because…" … "Then use it on yourself first. Before anyone… I want to be the one you tell." Oryn's new condition governs Tide reading outward: self first, then ask first every time. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B4] "You're the colour of the wall…"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:34:- **Day 110.** Lira first at the gate-walk at dusk, in the order he has had for fifteen days (protected exchange); the fighter's question ("It felt like a Third-day."); her hand along the plank to his boot; "Then six." **The circle of six**: what each of the four saw, in order; Karis's five findings said; Seln's "Yet."; Oryn's "I'm not going to guess past it."; nobody puts a verb between the facts; the four wheres; "We find the others…"; "One at a time, for money." Oryn: "North in the morning… Don't go in without me…"; her hand on Seln's shoulder. **Brom at the ladder** ("It's a count. You like counts."). **The Vastin window** (three sentences). **Oryn at the well**: the rule written while she watches (protected); "Once is a morning" (the debt's terms set by her: three readings on different days, then all of it at once); "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."; the note written under the rule. **The second pole** in the log (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:27:- **The council, the second honest collision:** Lira for walking away (the fence at forty and the walk at fifty, and pace the third circle on their own time); Brom ("Three hundred's a number a man doesn't reach for." — his father and the horse); Karis ("I would go alone."); **Seln: "Take it… People have faces. Six years I've wanted a face."** [OWNER-pending #50] Cael's sentence to the whole table (protected), then why: the assumption is wrong and cannot be known to be wrong. **Brom quotes Rooke**, the first person he has ever quoted: "Doors open both ways… I don't like it. I'm in." Lira: "I want it entered that I said walk away." The log (EXC-B7-002). Pike marks HOLD unasked and says it to the room. **Teague at the door** (protected): "If you're late back, we'll come look." / "Noted.", the first *Noted* to anyone above them on the wall.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:33:- **Day 115:** Teague holds the rim unasked ("We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted"). **C3: Karis paces the Stair's perimeter in the morning** with Lira one-armed on the line, under four rim-holders who are theirs, and gets two hundred. **Down with two lamps**: the air at the twentieth step; the chamber catalogued properly; Oryn's "What are they" / "Lines." **The kit**: open, contents in taking-out order, the cord laid toward the east wall, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar beside its mallet, point bright, the floor unmarked (EXC-B7-004: "Twice, by the head… Nothing goes into this."). **The ledger read by Seln**: distances, the radius in their own hand, a designation in an index he does not know, and the last line, *third site confirmed on bearing* —. **Karis's body at "bearing."** Six hours; twenty-nine sheets; "Sheet"; Lira ahead of her every time; **forty-one** (protected); the line *between* the courses at the radius; "A measurement is a fact about a ruler…" **The kit carried up**: Brom refuses help three times. The rim-holders: the spear grounded once. The log at the stone (protected). The straightedge out on the carter's map, not yet touching anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:28:- **The ledge and the stampede (≈4,500, terrain fight):** the ledge goes under Lira; her own Wind, full, crosses the gorge; thirty heads come up; the shelf cannot hold them at a run, and they come down the face in a front. "There. Thirty seconds. Lee side." "Cart's gone." **Karis's lattice line** across the face is a declaration the size of a road. The herd splits round the fin at eleven paces; she sits down at the eighth second, emptied. Brom goes back for two boxes (the wrist goes under the cloth). Cael goes after the third. Compression and Anchor *want*, and he prices both and holds, because the split stands on Karis's line and one more loud thing turns it. He takes the shoulder raw: three ribs, left side, low; the calf opened on the shale. The cart floats and goes in with its shafts up. Lira's leg broken under a plate, the boot gone. "That was me… The loud thing." / "It was the ledge. The ledge went. Then it was you." / "Then it was me."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:32:- **Oxhollow (day 84):** the table under the lean-to, hers twenty days at a time; worst first; "That's three." The map paid seventy ("Then they go round."). **The second and third readings** (ribs knitting with "nothing doing it"; the wrist and neck, nothing wrong, still nothing): "a river in the dark." **The two readings taught before they are load-bearing** (surface: a count of ten; deep: both hands, minutes, still and whole, at a mending's cost; "I don't run it on a road"). If the stall is named (C8 default: at most once), it is a limit she prices and hates, never used. **Three questions** (right places — yes; faster; no healer ever got anything — no). "That's the visit." He has a sentence asking her south and does not say it. "Thornwater's on my route in nine days… I want to read you when you're not broken." / "Nine days."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:25:- **The Drowned Hall from the rise:** roofless, twelve strides square, a spring through the broken floor, a marsh exactly as wide as the Quiet. "Third." **The line** at the marsh's edge ("Gone"/"Back"); **stake thirty-three** (old, and no second); mud **heaved from below** along the water's edge ("It's never been out."); a bar at the hall's lip **bent from below**, read from a hundred and eighty-five yards. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] **Oryn's lore**: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:29:- **Two days at the marsh (119–120):** two fires. Seln's blanket over Karis's shoulders. Lira keeps the bolt in the bow. Brom: "Twice." / "Twice." Oryn sleeps in front of people. **The second self-reading** (an hour; the banks a limit; **the still place**, named here for the first time; the river round a stone it has always known; four things he can count; protected log). The third before dawn: "the same." **Oryn changes the order**: "You in me." Asked and granted; surface, then a minute of the long one at her count, and while he is in, **he tells her exactly**; her finding (protected); "Write it down and stop touching it." **C3: Karis lays the cord at the Hall's perimeter** in the marsh between copies. **Teague's crew** along the track with a fifth: the older healer of no Path, "Twice?" / "Then it wants binding, not hands." The two women bind it. **Teague sits down beside him**, as Brom once did. "What are you." **The wrist a foot from his hand:** not the short reading, not the long one, not the asking. "Why did you stop reporting?" (protected exchange). "The board's going to need a new column." The log (protected). **The pencil stopping** at the far fire.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:43:- Lira's order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"). The ankle is unmended. Brom's shoulder is bound, not mended a third time. Oryn's crossbow is with Lira, with one bolt left.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:26:- **The board's room:** the wall rewritten, tenth; "Teague's nine up… He read that slip yesterday. Read it twice… I'd have done the same, and I told him, and he said he knew." **The council, once, in order:** Karis's case; Brom ("A survey kit's a cart's worth… That's not the reason. That's what it is."); Lira ("I'm saying it's a walk and a carry. I'm not saying it isn't the other thing."); Cael: "It pays."; **Seln reads the paper, not the words**: "Somebody wrote this who learned to write inside." / "It goes in." / "That's not a reason not to go." **The ninety-third**: nobody says *bring her*, and Karis writes "Thornwater, ninety-third. The healer." The Part-1 summary log (protected, "Twelve weeks").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:27:- **Day 91:** marked at the plank in front of eleven witnesses. The mail: **Ephram** and **Vell** (texts protected). **The void road (day 92):** the registry's printed sheet against the ground (seven dashed roads ending in white; this is the third); Karis's carter's map with three blank circles; "Their map has no roads. His has no quiet ground. Between them you get the country." Ephram's letter read at the wash at noon (Bracken told the registry "the Line and nothing past it"; Lira: "Good."). Vell's read at noon on the 94th, aloud, to Lira ("She puts the thing that decides it last." / "So does Ephram.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:30:- **Day 96, the perimeter (≈4,000, measured set piece):** procedure said once (Lira the instrument a stride inside; Karis on the line with the cord; Brom marking; Seln ahead; Oryn at the stone; Cael writing counts). The bend in Karis's wrist; **iron at the third cord**; sixty-two cords and twenty strides; ten cords to the middle; "A circle is a made shape." said once as geometry and not followed. **The stake**: registry stamp, thirty-one, a boot's width on the line, "Five years in the weather. A cold term either side."; "You drive them where you've measured to." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; restates protected Ch10 — OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:31:- **The trials at the stone:** Lira's full burst becomes a step ("It's in me. It's not in the air."; the clock line); Brom's "Skin."; Karis sees every point and can fill none ("It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend."); Seln vanishes for a breath without his Path ("It was never most of what I do."); **Oryn's three crossings** with Brom's arm in her hands ("Nothing in my hands" / "A healer's hands stop working there."). **Cael's two private tests:** the Iron read released before the stride, running across it; at twenty strides a foot's worth of Wind evasion round a stone. From behind it is a man stepping. "It was dark before. It's dark now." Both halves true; together not the truth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:24:- **The Ring (≈8,000–9,500 across two chapters), a retreat with a geometry.** The line is the objective. Nine counted on the white. "The road's cut." / "The grass. Where the cord went." Brom holds the lip: a hand's-height drop that robs a hound of drive, the haft, a man the pack cannot hear. Lira runs the rim's turned edge; the ankle goes a third time; the forearm taken and held; she cannot burst it off. **Brom's bolt through the eye at thirteen feet.** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] Oryn's hands: "Nothing… Nothing in my hands." Cloth and knees. "Move. I can't fix this here. Move." Brom's string opens his fingers in the dark. The lane counted down, 160 to 60, the scrub moving at Lira's pace and never showing a shape. They are *careless* in here, because no prey has ever shouted. **Karis down at sixty**, hands on a throat, the jaws closing across her fists, the loudest sound on the ring. **Shadow, once, ten strides**. Only Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln have the sightline; Oryn is screened by Brom and fixed on Lira/Karis, sees no discontinuity and cannot attribute the movement. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B2] The throw. Then *he stops holding*: Wind full, north off the lane; every head turns; then everything, one after another, so there is never a breath when he is not the loudest thing on the floor. Pressure for noise; Ember held out; Blade ringing with nothing to cut; Storm seeding the rut, the Iron/body read already released to the air and unavailable under his soles until the lane is relinquished [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B3]; Anchor off its hold and looking west. North to the rut, **east the wrong way** about a hundred and thirty yards, back west. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] Seln's "Back" from the stone and Lira's a breath after. The second lock with Compression at contact. Over the stone. **The bolt at six feet.** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] From within ten feet, Anchor's perception sees Karis's points before they light [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B1]: **the wall of ignition along the line's inside edge**, from her knees, voiceless. Seven break out north and south along the outside; two dead. Win-sentence and costs on the page. The opponent learned nothing it could use, because it had never needed to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:29:- **Day 100, the deep reading (≈4,500):** the back room fixed from the door (window, table, stool, the roll in her order); "Breathe like a man asleep."; the count of ten ("Nothing. As before."); then the long one. The current goes *along*, not down; she can be felt keeping time; her commentary on banks (Iron Skin walled, Ember hot, Wind too fast to feel), "there's more water"; Shadow draws in under her touch; Storm quiet; he understands she is not afraid of him, because her trade has no room for being impressed; "Eleven years…". **The conditions arrive.** He could stop it, and stopping would be the lie. *He reached. Directed. Open-eyed. Still.* **The notice, exactly.** Two firsts counted; the third not written. "Something just changed…" / "No. I did. I need to tell you what I am." / "Then lie still while you do it…"

