/bin/zsh -lc "for s in \"It's because you die,\" 'Four,' 'Out of five. Two men went down to that ford this month and one came up.' \"Seln did the shadow work tonight. I didn't. Out here there's a ledger and a ferry west once a month, and a defector's tradecraft in my hands would tell anyone who reads carefully where I learned it. The seal holds. Different country, same arithmetic.\" 'Stillhound pack, Thornwater ford: cleared. Five confirmed. Crew of five, four injured, none lost. Price paid.' \"First honest number anyone's written about us in a year. It says four of five got hurt. It's right.\" 'You mean the quiet ground?' 'Everybody knows the quiet ground. Nobody goes in.' \"So what am I becoming, exactly, if nobody's measuring?\" 'I keep waiting for someone to ask for my report.' 'What does the board pay a man with no Path at all.' 'Same as anyone,' \"What'd he do?\" \"Teague's still eleven up. He'll speak to you when you've cost him something.\" \"That's not rudeness. That's the ledger.\" \"Past the Line. Your grandmother crossed it once, before you were born, on a trade run; she said the roads were honest and the food wasn't. Mind the roads. Send word when there's a roof. — H.\"; do n="'$(rg -F -o -- "$s" editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-{08..14}.md | wc -l | tr -d '"' '); printf '%s :: %s\\n' \""'$n" "$s"; done' in /Users/drive/fractured-path-monroe13
