editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-11.md:165:He had written it in Hesk's book a dozen times, and had never before stood in it with something coming. *One*, and every fragment he owned went dumb. There were no hands to put down. For that one count he was a boy standing in a river with a knife, who could not have shifted his feet for the forty marks.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-11.md:415:*Deployment since the Line: one.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-12.md:29:*Fifty-fourth day. The ladder. Brom, one hand. Karis, elbows. Lira, seated, counting aloud. Mine, by the arms; the calf gives eleven strides on the flat and no rungs at all. Seln, as usual. The nine: idle, and asking. Deployment since the Line: one.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-12.md:229:"He's forty marks in his box against your coming," said the carter. "He told me to say that, and to say that he'd not paid a forty since the thaw." He scratched his neck. "I'm to tell you nothing about the top of his sheet, for there's nothing. The man wasn't down when I left."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-12.md:235:*Fifty-seventh day. Thornwater. Fifth line, in Pike's hand, by the carter. Forty marks, in his box. Earned, fifty-eight.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-12.md:245:*Deployment since the Line: one.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-12.md:265:So on the fifty-eighth morning she sat on the tail-board of a cart in Thornwater's yard with the calfskin unrolled beside her. She could not hold its corners down, and so Brom had brought four stones from the well's foot, and set one on each, and stepped back with his arm in its sling, looking as pleased as if he had been allowed to carry something.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-13.md:205:*Deployment since the Line: one.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-13.md:225:There were fourteen slips on the plank.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-13.md:287:"I've a line to say for you, and I've said it once already. And I've forty marks in that box." He swung the sack onto the plank. "But the ferry's in, and it's mail first. It's always mail first. There's people in this meadow have waited a month to hear their name."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:1:# Chapter 14 — Twelfth
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:77:*Deployment since the Line: one.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:101:"Earned, fifty-eight," said Karis. "In hand, forty-eight."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:119:"Twelfth," said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:139:"He must have said something. We took forty marks off him."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:151:"Teague's still eleven up. He'll speak to you when you've cost him something." Pike set down his cup. "That's not rudeness. That's the ledger."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:415:"Shut isn't sound. There's a difference, and I mean to hear it before I pick anything up." He tucked in the end with his teeth. "I've stood about for thirteen days, and I can stand about a few more."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:441:*Six lines in Pike's book. The sixth is a well: air cleared, shaft drawn, six stones set. Earned, sixty-two. In hand, fifty-two. Twelfth of thirteen. The top line is eleven up, and its captain has been in and gone out again on two holds' slips, and has said nothing to us or about us. Pike says that is the ledger.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:451:*Deployment since the Line: one.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-10.md:37:And it was dusk. He had known that it would be, and had thought of little else for the whole mile down. Shadow lifted behind the rest, soft, as it had lifted at every dusk for fifty days, with the one offer that he had ever wanted to take; and tonight he must stand still for an hour with it at his shoulder, in a place where being less would have been worth more than forty marks.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-09.md:9:It was strange to walk that mile for a third reason. He had gone up it once behind a cart, for nine marks, with a grey thing pacing him; and he had come down it at noon behind the same cart empty, when it was nothing but grass. Now he went up it in the afternoon with a forty-mark slip in his shirt, toward a gate whose keeper had sent for somebody else. The ground was the same each time. What changed was the thing he had come to do on it, and he was beginning to think that this was the only sort of change of which the country out here took any notice.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-09.md:317:He wrote the day while Brom trimmed the wick. *Fifty-second day. Thornwater. Seven at the ford, by Seln's count, and one of them lies on the bar. Karis has a hypothesis, in two clauses, and tomorrow at dusk we test both. If I spend anything it will be Wind, once, where it can be seen. Deployment since the Line: none.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:37:He went over it once, the tents and the carts and the three fires, where thirteen crews were getting their breakfasts or pretending to; and then he went over it a second time, more slowly. On the second pass his eyes came to five people standing by a dead fire with their blankets still on the grass. They rested there, and went on to the end of the meadow, and came back.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:115:Cael watched the feather go back behind his ear, and understood what he had just seen done. That book was thirty years of a single question, which was who had come back, and every crew Pike had ever sent down a road had either proved him right or was not there to prove him wrong. In all that time he had said yes to one hold. This morning he had struck it with his own pen, before two hundred people, and written beneath it the mark of the lowest line on his wall; and if five strokes did not come up from that river, it would not be Teague's name that the meadow remembered beside the forty marks.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:131:They were over the saddle before the mist had lifted, with a mark's worth of flour and bacon in the bag and nine marks left in Karis's purse.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:133:The road was the one they knew. It went down into the grey scrub in two ruts, and the cart fitted them as before; the three boxes rode on the sacks under their own canvas, and Karis walked at the off wheel. They passed the wash in the middle of the morning, dry and red, with its thorn stump on the eastern lip. They kept the hold without thinking of it, and Lira's knife and Brom's bill rode where a stranger could see them. In nearly every particular it was the walk they had made ten days ago for nine marks.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:167:*In hand, nine.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:169:*Deployment since the Line: none.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:173:"Thirteenth of thirteen," she said at last. "Sent for the forty. Do you know what that would be, at home? It'd be the bottom seed drawn against the title in the first round, because the title was out of town. Iron against Gold, and no panel to tell you so."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:209:"I go at my hour," he said. "I've done that for twenty-two years and I'll not stop for forty marks of somebody else's. I'll have your boxes in her loft before the sun's over." He looked at the bar, and then at the five of them, and Cael thought that he had something more to say. But all he did was nod, once, at Brom, as a man nods who has lent a tool.

