+# Verdict: RATIFY WITH LINE FIXES
+
+Scope: twelve local replacements in chapters 9, 10, 12, and 13. They (a) keep Karis's water clause hypothetical until the fight supplies evidence, (b) restore the protected quiet-ground utterance as one uninterrupted three-sentence unit, (c) restore the source context of "They stop inside, where the tiers are"—*they* are healers, not ranks—and repair Lira's later reference, and (d) restore terminal punctuation on two packet-quoted sentences. No structural rewrite, fight cut, calendar change, canon deletion, or name request is required.
+
+## 1. Continuity with the closed text
+
+**PASS after the listed line fixes. No contradiction with Movement 1 survives.**
+
+- Entry state is continuous: Movement 1 ends on day 49 with four lines, thirteenth of thirteen, about ten marks, all five uninjured, nine fragments plus the anomaly, and no deployment (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:269-289`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:238-250`). Movement 2 opens on day 51, spends one mark, retains thirteenth, and records nine in hand and no deployment (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:131-173`). Day 50 is an intentional off-page day, not a missing counted day (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:31-33`).
+- The ford placement fits the closed route. On day 43 the party crossed two unnamed shallow fords before reaching the stretch (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:99-103`); Thornwater was fixed as two party-days from Lowmarch (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:217-223`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:201`). The upper crossing is walked on day 52 (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:185-215`) and is two to three hours below the gate in the Movement 2 travel (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:3-13`). No later packet relocates it.
+- The stillhound sense remains unknown through Movement 1: Cael can prove only that the animal tracked the buckle and cannot name the sense (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:229-247`); Seln's private conclusion is only that it waits on an unknown signal (`manuscript/chapter-06.md:127-139`). Movement 2 puts the discharge/water model in a leaf explicitly headed *Hypothesis; ... not tested* (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:189-213`), then obtains the evidence in the fight (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:55-95`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:245-257`) and enters a five-sentence finding afterward, in Cael's hand at Karis's dictation (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:357-397`). Chapter 10:25 alone overstates the result before the test; fix 2 makes it conditional.
+- Cael's deployment account is exact: none on days 51 and 52 (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:165-169`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:317`), one Wind burst on day 53 (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:157-165,401-415`), and one thereafter (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:29,235-245`; `manuscript/chapter-13.md:201-205`; `manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-451`). Cael refuses his Shadow-adjacent fragment (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:23,37-39`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:151-165,407-415`). Seln's submerged use is his native Shadow Path (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:19-25`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:177,245`), so it neither changes Cael's count nor violates Cael's seal (`BOOK_MAP.md:180-188`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:199`).
+- Bodies reconcile into Movement 3: Cael's calf ends flat/nine uphill, Brom's wrist closed but not sound, Lira's ankle stiff and unmended, and Karis's palms pink (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:403-443`), exactly matching the next packet's entry (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:16-18`). Seln remains unmarked (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:317-325`). No healer or Tide practitioner appears; the steading woman supplies ordinary wound care, and the only available-healer statement is that the nearest walks a route and is not due (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:281-315`).
+- Money is exact: about ten at handoff (`manuscript/chapter-07.md:269-279`), nine after day-51 provisions (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:131,165-169`), forty-eight after the hold's one mark and the forty-mark ford payment (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:19-23`; `manuscript/chapter-14.md:81-105`), then fifty-two after the well (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:339-343,439-451`). Earned total is 18 + 40 + 4 = 62 (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:235`; `manuscript/chapter-14.md:441`).
+- Assets remain continuous: the three boxes travel on the Thornwater cart and return to the ferry loft (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:123-133`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:111-171`; `manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-449`); the reserve is never opened; Seln's case spends only the fight evening in Thornwater's loft and returns to his strap (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:17`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:142-144`). Brom's hedging bill, Lira's long knife, Karis's carter map and archive, and Hesk's satchel remain accounted for (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:143-163`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:111-171`; `manuscript/chapter-14.md:27-75`). The bowman's ash stick is the prop under the carter's shaft (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:345-359`); it is not Brom's older ash wedge, which remains unspent from Movement 1 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:248`).
+- Board state is continuous: the ford becomes the fifth line on day 57 and the well the sixth; the crew rises to twelfth while Teague remains eleven above (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:193-245`; `manuscript/chapter-14.md:109-151,439-451`). Teague returns on day 57, reads the struck slip and their line, then leaves on two hold slips without a meeting (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:129-151`), satisfying the absence ruling (`packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:49-55`).
+
+## 2. The movement plan and AUTHOR-REPORT flags
+
+The required beat order is complete: struck HOLD and acceptance (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:43-119`); ford walked (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:185-301`); lore, seven, hypothesis, and plan (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:55-317`); point, test, pack learning, seam, one Wind burst, and Seln's cut (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:55-175`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:3-199`); costs, witness, finding, and seal log (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:217-415`); recovery and quiet-ground rumor (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:3-357`); road-down question and Lowmarch board scenes (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:3-345`); letter, wall, well, recovery, and closing tack (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:3-465`). Nothing reserved to a later movement is spent.
+
+Owner-flag rulings:
+
+| Flag | Ruling | Audit |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1. Fight length | **KEEP** | The point-to-downstream sequence is about 6,900 words, above the 4,500–5,500 allowance (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:111`; `BOOK_MAP.md:202-220`), but the excess is earned: chapter 10 carries the declared-bait demonstrations and the full Lira window (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:55-287`), while chapter 11 carries opponent learning, the first-mover deduction, the priced burst, and the downstream/open count (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:3-199`). The whole movement is only 806 words over its 36,000 budget (`AUTHOR-REPORT.md:7,36`). Cutting to the allowance would remove planned learning rather than repetition. |
+| 2. Ford placement/timing | **KEEP** | The upper day-43 crossing is compatible with the two unnamed crossings and the two-day road (`manuscript/chapter-05.md:99-103`; `manuscript/chapter-06.md:217-223`). It is walked on day 52 and fought on day 53 (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:187`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:3-55`). No later packet conflicts. |
+| 3. The third/lip stones | **KEEP** | The third is explicitly a man of the hold, one of the annual stone setters; the row is restored whole on the return (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:43-59`; `manuscript/chapter-13.md:53-61`). No name is minted. |
+| 4. Seln's Shadow under water | **KEEP** | It is Seln's native Path and tests Karis's water clause (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:189-213,287-305`; `manuscript/chapter-10.md:19-25`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:245-247`). The seal governs Cael's Shadow-adjacent fragment, which he refuses (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:407-415`). Later packets remain consistent: Seln can vanish by craft without his Path at the Quiet line (`packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:30-31`). |
+| 5. “They stop inside…” as ranks | **AMEND** | The manuscript expressly says *they* means ranks (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:33-45,185`), but the source's full protected unit makes the antecedent healers: “Healer would've… / There isn't one. / There's not. They stop…” (`books/book-07-void-roads/chapters/chapter-04.md:67-74`). Fixes 5–11 restore the exact source dialogue and preserve Lira's later protected question without changing its words. |
