+## 4. Standing defaults and Reader Standard
+
+**PASS after the protected-context fixes.**
+
+- Chapters 8–14 contain no named season, named month, English weekday, metric unit, or count of years since Kindling. Generic *month*, *thaw*, and *frost* are permitted (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:333`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:229`; `manuscript/chapter-14.md:5,157,255`). Distances use feet, yards, paces, and strides (`manuscript/chapter-08.md:187-215`; `manuscript/chapter-09.md:279`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:245`).
+- Cael is eighteen, matching the ledger (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:49`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:238`).
+- No use of “his Path” refers to Cael. The phrase refers to Brom or Seln (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:251`; `manuscript/chapter-11.md:177,245`); Cael consistently has fragments (`manuscript/chapter-10.md:23`; `manuscript/chapter-14.md:243-247,447-451`).
+- The ford witness is unambiguous for a thirteen-year-old reader: the survivor put his hand between the jaws and his throat, rather than harming himself (`manuscript/chapter-09.md:83-109`). Injury is consequential but not dwelt on as gore (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:217-237,281-315`). The well's count-and-call sequence makes the danger and the correct decision legible (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:233-305`).
